    "result_text": "Full suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derivation as a server-side computed field, matching how the existing `initials` and `membershipNumber` fields are handled \u2014 pure derivations from persisted `Owner` fields, computed at response-mapping time.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```\n   SILVER when namesakeCount == 0 && email is present, otherwise BRONZE\n   ```\n   The null/empty guards keep it safe when `namesakeCount` or `email` is absent (which correctly yields `BRONZE`).\n\nBoth `Cp15Tests` cases pass \u2014 `SILVER` for a unique owner with an email, `BRONZE` when no email is present \u2014 and the full suite (25 tests) remains green.",
